## Compatibility finding and change

- `MQClientManager.getOrCreateProduceAccumulator(ClientConfig)` caches by
  `ClientConfig.buildMQClientId()`. The invoked Java fixture records same-ID
  accumulator reuse and distinct-ID separation. Fixture SHA-256:
  `e285d6e3408c9824feb957fb8cbf16f0209c9b345343a6db8a1ca3a954f40eba`.
- Rust now caches the shared accumulator by explicit manager identity and the
  Java-compatible client ID. Producer instances share live thresholds, queued
  batches and worker state. Each pending batch retains its first Producer as
  the send owner. Shutdown stops workers without discarding queued entries;
  later Producer startup resumes workers and schedules retained deadlines.
- `auto_batch_is_shared_by_client_id_and_keeps_first_producer_owner` verifies
  fixture identity, same/different IDs, shared live settings, first-owner
  transport routing and restart behavior.
  `stopped_accumulator_retains_pending_batches_for_restart` verifies queued
  entries and original deadlines survive stop and become ready after restart.
- Updated the Phase 6 API map, Phase 6 requirement audit and Phase 7 Producer
  matrix. The general offline benchmark sample is recorded separately.

